{% set sections = [
  ["Introduction & Scope", "This Privacy Policy explains how Elysium+ collects, uses, shares and protects personal data when you visit this website, contact us, apply for or take part in one of our activities, or otherwise interact with our network across Ukraine, Poland, Italy and Germany. It applies to visitors of this website as well as to members, volunteers, participants and partners of Elysium+. We aim to handle personal data responsibly, transparently and in line with applicable data protection law, including the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) where it applies to us, and Ukrainian data protection legislation."],
  ["Who We Are", "Elysium+ is a non-profit youth organisation registered in Ukraine, working on inclusion, non-formal education, digital empowerment and youth mobility, with branches in Poland, Italy and Germany. For data protection purposes, Elysium+ acts as the Data Controller for personal data processed through this website and our activities. Registered address: Peremohy Avenue 119A, apt. 307, 14000 Chernihiv, Ukraine. Contact for all data protection matters: contact@elysium.ngo."],
  ["What Personal Data We Collect", "When you contact us, subscribe to updates, or otherwise reach out, we collect what you provide directly — typically your name, email address, and the content of your message. If you apply to take part in an exchange, training or other activity, we may additionally collect information such as date of birth, nationality, passport or ID details needed for travel and visa purposes, dietary or accessibility needs, and emergency contact details, where relevant to that specific activity. We also collect limited technical data automatically when you browse this website (such as IP address, device and browser type, pages visited, and approximate city/country-level location) as described in the Cookies & Analytics section below. We do not intentionally collect special categories of data (such as health, religious or political information) unless you choose to share it with us, for example to request accessibility support."],
  ["Children and Young People", "Elysium+ works with young people, some of whom may be under 18. Where an activity involves a participant who is a minor under applicable law, we require the consent of a parent or legal guardian before collecting or processing that participant's personal data, and we take extra care in how that data is handled, shared and retained. If you believe we hold data about a minor without appropriate consent, please contact us immediately at contact@elysium.ngo."],
  ["How We Use Your Data & Our Legal Bases", "We use personal data to: respond to enquiries; organise, run and report on projects and activities; administer volunteer, membership and donor relationships; send updates where you have opted in; and maintain and improve this website. Depending on the purpose, we rely on one or more of the following legal bases: your consent (which you may withdraw at any time); the performance of a contract or arrangement with you (for example, registering you for an activity); our legitimate interests in running the organisation responsibly; and compliance with a legal obligation, including reporting obligations to funders such as the European Commission or national Erasmus+ agencies."],
  ["Cookies & Analytics", "This website does not currently use any analytics, advertising or tracking tools — no browsing behaviour is tracked. The only thing stored in your browser is a single strictly-necessary entry in local storage that remembers the choice you make in the cookie banner, so we don't ask you again on every visit; it contains no personal data and isn't used to track you. If we ever introduce analytics or tracking, we will update this Policy first and ask for your specific, informed consent via an on-screen notice — describing what's being added and why — before anything non-essential runs. You can review or change your saved preference at any time via \"Cookie preferences\" in the footer."],
  ["How We Store and Protect Your Data", "Personal data is stored securely with hosting and email providers that apply appropriate technical and organisational safeguards, including encrypted connections and access restrictions. We keep personal data only for as long as necessary for the purpose it was collected: general enquiries are typically kept for up to 2 years; records of participants in a funded activity may be kept for up to 5 years, or longer where a funder's reporting rules require it. Exact retention periods depend on the activity and applicable donor requirements."],
  ["Sharing of Your Data", "We do not sell or rent personal data. We share it only where necessary: with hosting and email service providers who process data on our behalf; with partner organisations and funding or accrediting bodies (such as national Erasmus+ agencies) when needed to administer or report on a joint activity; or with public authorities where we are legally required to. Any third party processing personal data on our behalf is required to protect it to a comparable standard."],
  ["International Data Transfers", "Elysium+ is established in Ukraine, which has not been recognised by the European Commission as providing an adequate level of data protection. If you are located in the European Economic Area (EEA) and interact with us, your personal data will typically be processed in Ukraine. Where this applies, we rely on appropriate safeguards recognised under GDPR — such as Standard Contractual Clauses or your explicit, informed consent — for that transfer."],
  ["Automated Decision-Making", "We do not use automated decision-making or profiling that produces legal effects or otherwise significantly affects you. Decisions about participation in our activities are made by people."],
  ["Your Rights", "Depending on where you live, you may have the right to: access the personal data we hold about you; request that it be corrected or deleted; restrict or object to certain processing; withdraw consent at any time; and receive a copy of your data in a portable format. To exercise any of these rights, contact us at contact@elysium.ngo. If you are not satisfied with our response, you may lodge a complaint with your national data protection authority (for example, your EU member state's authority) or, in Ukraine, with the Ukrainian Parliament Commissioner for Human Rights (Ombudsperson)."],
  ["Data Breach Notification", "If a personal data breach occurs that is likely to pose a risk to your rights or freedoms, we will notify the relevant supervisory authority and, where required, the individuals affected, within the timeframes required by applicable law."],
  ["Links to Other Websites", "Our website may link to external sites, such as partners, funders or social media platforms. We are not responsible for their privacy practices, and we encourage you to review their policies before sharing any personal information with them."],
  ["Changes to This Policy", 'We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or in the law. Material changes will be reflected on this page with an updated "last updated" date above.'],
  ["Contact Us", "For any question, comment or request related to your personal data or this Policy, contact Elysium+ at contact@elysium.ngo, or write to us at our registered address above."]
] %}

